		<SimpleData name="aggregated_crossings_id">6971</SimpleData>
		<SimpleData name="guppy_notes">2006.072 Pine River oxbow Hwy 97 MoT S1 RC Outlet drop, River oxbow cut off by highway fill. Deep, wide fill - Install 30 m bridge with 20+ m wide channel, in oxbow culvert length; major project to excavate. Old natural channel conjunction with providing water flow from the inlet beaver lodge connection to river at 543878 6162821. Culvert end of the oxbow (site 2006.071). A bridge is covers inlet. plugged. Two similar oxbows are present 10-12 km needed to ensure upstream fish passage into the further east along Highway 97 -- they have similar oxbow during high water flows. Install a 0.5 m high opportunities for reconnection with the Pine River. rock weir about 2 metres back from the crossing structure inlet without impeding fish passage, to discourage beaver dam construction right at the inlet. Extend the surface of the new stream channel to the top of the weir, resulting in a shallow pool above the upstream end of the new channel. 17</SimpleData>
	</SchemaData></ExtendedData>
      <Point><coordinates>-122.301026,55.610956</coordinates></Point>
