		<SimpleData name="guppy_notes">2006.291 Sukunka River 200 MoF S3 RC Culvert width; Shallow road fill; culvert with hole in top from Determine fish use. If there is fish use, install (1) trib. Road km outlet drop grader. Fish in plunge pool (dead sculpin and live 10 m bridge with 5+ m channel width or (2) 6+ m 46.5 minnows - probably NSC). Connectivity confirmed - wide x 16 m long open-bottom arch. The road fill is side channel of Sukunka immediately downstream. very shallow, construct the new channel so that the Previous 2 sites are the same stream. Spring (RB) surface is at the level of the plunge pool surface to spawning potential. accommodate the crossing structure. Slope the channel upstream from the crossing structure at &lt; 5% gradient.</SimpleData>
	</SchemaData></ExtendedData>
